.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
# openWakeWord downloads its pretrained models here on first run -- those are
# re-fetched automatically, so they stay out. Custom-trained models are not
# recoverable that way, so they must be tracked or a fresh clone loses the
# wake word.
models/*
!models/*.onnx
!models/*.tflite
*.wav
!assets/*.wav
# training-samples/ holds recordings of the owner's voice, used to pin the
# wake-word thresholds. Deliberately NOT tracked: this repository is public,
# and a recording of someone's voice is not the kind of thing to publish for
# the convenience of a test fixture.
#
# The wake-word tests skip themselves when the samples are absent, so a fresh
# clone gets a green suite. To restore that coverage on your own machine, put
# your own recordings here -- 16 kHz mono WAV, one saying the wake word, one
# saying similar phrases that are not it -- and see tests/test_wake_word.py.
state/
